    "answer": {
      "short": "$100$; $25$ groups, each with sum $4$.",
      "worked": "Group consecutive terms in fours. The first group gives\n$$\\begin{align*}100+99-98-97&=199-195\\\\100+99-98-97&=4\\end{align*}$$\nEach successive group also has sum $4$, ending with $4+3-2-1=4$. There are $100$ terms, so\n$$\\begin{align*}100\\div4&=25\\\\25\\times4&=100\\end{align*}$$",
